 # Marching Tetrahedrons Algorithm
-
-
 ## Overview
-The Marching Tetrahedrons Algorithm (MTA) is an iso-surface extraction method that converts a volumetric grid into a polygonal mesh by decomposing each cubic cell into tetrahedra and determining intersections within them [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the shared principles of [Cell projection](26-cell-projection.md) but distinguishes itself from its sibling [Marching Cubes](26-cell-projection.md) by resolving topological ambiguities inherent in cubic decomposition through specific tetrahedral tessellation patterns [S1, unofficial]. Unlike [Projected Tetrahedra](877-projected-tetrahedra.md) which projects primitives to screen space, MTA operates in object space to generate a watertight manifold [S1, unofficial].
-
