 ### [Subgrid Pipeline](1640-subgrid-pipeline.md)
-The Subgrid Pipeline is a method for extracting isosurfaces from tetrahedral grids by resolving topological ambiguities within individual tetrahedra using subgrid-accurate intersection data. It distinguishes itself from standard MTA by explicitly handling open, scoop, and normal boundary curves to ensure watertightness, allowing multiple intersection vertices per edge to represent complex topology. It builds on [Marching Tetrahedrons Algorithm](940-marching-tetrahedrons-algorithm.md) by replacing the fixed lookup table with a local reconstruction procedure that processes boundary curves. Choose this for complex topologies where standard MTA fails to capture fine details. [Subgrid Pipeline](1640-subgrid-pipeline.md)
